cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Cerebro P4: AI research on the ESP32-P4"
abstract: >-
  How much AI fits in a US$15 microcontroller: the ESP32-P4 receives the PC camera over USB, runs three neural networks (faces, people, cats; ESPDet-Pico with ESP-DL and PIE), tracks the face with the PPA and returns a 1080p UVC webcam in MJPEG and H.264, plus a USB network dashboard and hardware-accelerated HTTPS. Measured finding: PSRAM bandwidth (~300 MB/s) is the ceiling, not the accelerators.
